      "Wealth-related observances are therefore the core of its reputation. A Lakshmi puja, registering property, buying a vehicle or jewellery and a Kuber yantra worship are the examples given, with the morning favoured for the latter. In a notable twist, detachment rites and a vairagya sankalp are listed as things to avoid, since a yoga of material comfort is ill matched to an act of renunciation. It is an honest reminder that the panchang treats worldly and ascetic aims as different and assigns them different days.",
      "In the order of the cycle, it follows the cautionary Vyatipata, which gives a recognisable pattern of calamity followed by plenty. As with any almanac statement, the real span depends on the sun and moon's longitudes where you are, and customs vary in how strictly the guidance is applied. Prosperity in practice depends on income, care and judgment, and a favourable yoga is at most a traditional nod to good timing for those who enjoy observing it.",
