      "The twentieth yoga is named Shiva, a word meaning auspicious, kind or benign, which is also the name of one of the great deities of the tradition. One point is worth stating plainly because it surprises many readers. In most almanacs the presiding deity of this yoga is Mitra, not Shiva himself, and the nature is auspicious. The name reflects the adjective as much as the god.",
