      "It follows the cautionary Parigha and is followed by Siddha, so it opens a long run of favourable yogas that continues through most of the rest of the cycle. The pattern is a good example of how almanacs describe time as a rhythm of rough and smooth stretches. Whether or not you hold the calendar as binding, it offers a vocabulary for talking about the quality of a day. Spans vary by location and almanac, so check a local source for the dates relevant to you, and treat the guidance as custom and not as any promise of results.",
