      "Shubha is the twenty-third yoga, and the name is the everyday Sanskrit word for auspicious or good. The same word is part of the vocabulary of every Indian wedding invitation and festival greeting, from shubh vivah to shubh deepavali. The deity listed for it is Lakshmi, the goddess of fortune and prosperity, and the nature is auspicious.",
