      "Shukla, the twenty-fourth yoga, shares its name with the bright half of the lunar month, the shukla paksha, but this is a different thing. As an adjective the word means bright, white or pure, and in the yoga series it is the interval at which the combined sun and moon longitudes pass through that numbered slice. The deity in most almanacs is Parvati, the consort of Shiva, and the nature is auspicious.",
